d physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  consent was obtained  2 aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles without  anesthesia and without complications  1 slide was stained for immediate  evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were not discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Dr  Specht in person          Electronically Signed Out By  Rosemary H Tambouret MD on REMOVED_DATE 12 41       CLINICAL HISTORY    Left breast lump self discovered    Core biopsy done but uncertain if enough tissue obtained        SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 1 slide in ETOH and 1 air dried slide     B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  name and  medical number   REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a collodion bag  Entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  casette           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Specimen  BREAST CELLBLOCK  LEFT       report_end  , Unchecked.
