Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 MAY 01 ACCESSIONED ON  10 MAY 01 at 13 14 CLINICAL DATA  Extensive DCIS with positive margins on an outside hospital biopsy  not reviewed here                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL    REMOVED_CASE_ID    BIOPSY  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Scattered small nests of cytokeratin positive tumor cells are present within the subcapsular and medullary sinuses of one node by immunostains of three levels of block A  No cytokeratin positive cells are seen by immunostains of three levels of block B  and no convincing tumor cells are seen on the frozen section or permanent H    E  stained sections  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   476   BIOPSY  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ONE NODE   SEE NOTE  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  The immunostains of each of three levels of block C show scattered small nests of cytokeratin positive tumor cells within the subcapsular sinus  BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   TOTAL MASTECTOMY AND REGIONAL LYMPH NODE DISSECTION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  NUCLEAR GRADE 3 OF 3  SEE NOTE  2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  GRADE 2 TO 3 OF 3  JUST OUTSIDE THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE  INVOLVING 15 OF 25 SECTIONS AND SPANNING UP TO REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST LINEAR DIMENSION  MEASURED FROM EE   MARGINS NEGATIVE FOR TUMOR  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  SMALL HAMARTOMA  5  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 4 OF 4 AXILLARY NODES  NOTE  Most of the breast is fibrotic and no discrete mass is seen grossly  The dye discolored area around the biopsy site is extensively sampled  and a single focus of invasive tumor measuring 0 1cm in greatest dimension is identified on section FF  Because of minute dimensions  the grade is assigned based upon the nuclear features  No lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is seen  The previous excision is not available for review  The margins are negative for tumor  BREAST  RIGHT AXILLARY  ADDITIONAL   BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 01 at 19 19                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block FF   The tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  25 MAY 01 at 14 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are four specimens  Labelled  right hot blue  sentinel node   REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of yellow fibrofatty soft tissue containing 2 tan  rubbery lymph nodes each measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Both nodes are frozen entirely as fx 1  resubmitted as A  The remaining fibrofatty tissue is submitted entirely as B  Labelled  right sentinel node  476  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan rubbery node frozen entirely as fx 2  resubmitted as C  The third specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm mastectomy  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ellipse of unremarkable skin with an unremarkable 3 0cm nipple  The specimen is oriented by a short suture designating the superior and long suture designating the lateral margins  Attached is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tail  The specimen is black inked and serially sectioned to reveal a medially located REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm cavitary lesion lined by tan pink smooth membranous tissue and surrounded by fat necrosis with blue injected dye  This lesion abuts all the inked margins  The remainder of parenchyma is remarkable for very firm rubbery white fibrous tissue extending to all inked margins  The axillary tail is serially sectioned to reveal multiple nodes and white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted  SECTION CODE  D  deep and superior E  deep and medial F  cavity medial and inferior G  anterior portion of fibrous tissue adjacent to cavity and superior H  anterior inferior fibrous tissue I  deep central J  lateral and deep K  medial and superior L  medial and inferior M  central and anterior N  central and deep O  one lymph node bisected P  multiple lymph nodes Q  fibrous tissue R  O 5cm nodule within fibrous tissue  W  cavity  deep lateral X JJ  additional sections near biopsy site  Labelled  additional right axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm unoriented tan yellow fibrofatty portion of breast serially sectioned and submitted entirely as S T  Resident  SOHEIL DADRAS  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LYMPH NODE  RIGHT SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2 LYMPH NODE  RIGHT SENTINEL  476   RARE ATYPICAL CELLS IN SINUS  DIFFER TO PERMANENT SECTIONS  DISCUSSED WITH DR  SMITH  O R  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Y