E_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  and unit number only  is a 39 x 23 x 4 5cm simple mastectomy specimen oriented by the surgeon with stitch on axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 14 5cm attached skin ellipse with a nipple areolar complex 6cm in diameter with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm everted nipple  There is a well healed curved scar 6cm in length  curving around the medial aspect of the areola  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue and posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a 4 x 3 x 1 7cm cavity site located in the inner upper quadrant  The closest posterior margin is 2 5cm away  and the closest anterior margin is 4cm away from the cavity  In the section immediately lateral to the biopsy cavity site  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm tan nodule  5 5cm from the closest posterior margin  and 4cm from the closest anterior margin  No lymph nodes are identified on palpation of the axillary tail  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior margin to nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule in its entirety   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from cavity site  including closest posterior resection margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section lower outer quadrant  Received in formalin  labeled  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue dissected to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 7cm candidate lymph node  mostly replaced by adipose tissue  The candidate lymph node is bisected and submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining adipose tissue is submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Friday February 13   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 07 13PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies