arkable fibrofatty tissue and no masses or lesions are grossly identified  Sectioning of the axillary region does not reveal lymph nodes  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Surgical site  submitted from lateral to medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the central breast region  submitted from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper outer breast quadrant  Also received in the same specimen container is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of tan red fibrofatty tissue which is sectioned to reveal no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections of this additional specimen are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh labeled  right simple mastectomy   is a 560 gr   REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 4cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by an REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm irregular portion of tan pink skin with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan unremarkable nipple  which is 1 0cm from the superior margin  A short black stitch designates the superior margin and a long black stitch designates the lateral margin of the specimen  The anterior margin is inked blue and the posterior one black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an upper outer quadrant REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan yellow clear serous fluid filled surgical cavity  which is lined by chalky yellow fat necrosis and hemorrhage  The cavity abuts the posterior margin and is 0 4cm from the anterior margin of the specimen  Also noted  0 4cm medial to the surgical cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm bright yellow orange focus of fat necrosis  This nodule is 3 4cm from the posterior margin  The remaining cut surfaces of the specimen display diffuse gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesion or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the axillary region reveals no palpable lymph nodes  R